#====================================================================
# E262 — Classify scratch aliases before strict parent resolution
#====================================================================

id:                     E262
trigger_tool:           native-image|python|runtime|test_package
phase:                  runtime|testing
error_signature:        FileNotFoundError:.*\.t|Native Image output directory is missing:.*scratch|Native Image output must not use scratch path|scratch-alias

severity:               3
category:               filesystem|symlink|scratch|path-policy|security
match_keywords:         native-image, scratch, symlink, policy resolver, missing parent, .t, reserved output, path classification
title:                  Reserved scratch aliases must be classified before strict parent resolution

root_cause:             An output path can traverse a symlink into a reserved scratch tree whose final parent does not yet exist. Strict resolution fails with FileNotFoundError before the safety policy classifies the alias, so a security rejection is misreported as an ordinary missing-directory error.
affected_scope:         Build wrappers and code generators that reserve a fixed scratch subtree, reject outputs inside it, and accept user-provided destinations that may traverse symbolic links.
verification_cmd:       Create scratch-alias pointing to a missing .t directory and require the reserved-scratch error; use an unrelated missing parent as a control and require the ordinary missing-directory error.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           policy-first-nonstrict-resolution
rec_description:        When strict parent resolution fails, walk components with a bounded non-strict policy resolver, follow links explicitly, detect loops, and classify whether the destination resolves into the reserved scratch tree before emitting the ordinary missing-parent error.
rec_command:            Resolve the candidate parent and cwd/.t with the policy-only resolver, then pass scratch aliases to the existing safe-destination gate.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      reject-unresolved-symlink-destinations
fallback_description:   If a bounded non-strict resolver is unavailable, fail closed on unresolved destinations containing symlink components rather than treating them as ordinary missing parents.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       Path\(.*\)\.resolve\(strict=True\).*scratch|except FileNotFoundError:.*missing
forbid_1_reason:        Strict resolution before policy classification hides a reserved scratch alias behind a generic missing-directory error.
forbid_1_consequence:   Security tests exercise the wrong terminal class and callers cannot distinguish policy rejection from an absent directory.

principles:             P017

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E262.md
last_updated:           2026-08-08
source_event:           GraalVM 25.0.3 PR #3928 reserved Native Image scratch alias failure

authors:                2301_80739235 <2047361658@qq.com>
